# Commercially-licensed font faces — NOT redistributable via this repo.
#
# Joe Hand is licensed for web embedding (JOEBOB graphics Webfont EULA 1.0, licence owner
# Southern Destinations) and its §1.3 pageview cap was accepted by the client on
# 2026-09-09 — but §1.5 forbids direct download/hotlinking and §1.6 forbids transfer or
# sublicensing, and a repository is a distribution channel. So the face is delivered by
# the build/deploy pipeline rather than committed. This is about redistribution, not
# doubt: the rights themselves are confirmed. → assets/fonts/LICENCES.md
#
# ⚠️ A fresh clone has 1 unresolved @font-face rule until the pipeline supplies the file.
# The `accent` family falls back to La Belle Aurore (bundled) and then cursive — degraded,
# not broken.
#
# ⚠️ These patterns do not remove the files already in git history. If this repo is ever
# public again, history needs rewriting. See CHANGELOG.md → Security.
#
# No Optima face is registered or bundled: the three previously here were unlicensed and
# were removed 2026-08-18. SD now holds two *desktop* Optima licences (MyFonts #9528082
# and #7491875209386) and no webfont licence — the 2026 order's EULA forbids server
# installation and defines OTF→WOFF2 conversion as a prohibited Derivative Work. The
# optima-* pattern therefore guards a plausible mistake, not a theoretical one: 12 desktop
# OTFs sit in the workspace and woff2_compress is installed. → LS-2641
#
# The OFL/Apache faces (Open Sans, Belleza, La Belle Aurore) are committed and safe to ship.
assets/fonts/optima-*.woff2
assets/fonts/joe-hand-*.woff2

# Test artefacts
tests/**/test-results/
tests/**/playwright-report/
tests/**/node_modules/
